<h3 class='sec-banner' style='margin-top:16px;color:#1e1b4b;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;padding-bottom:4px;page-break-after:avoid;'>Section A: Multiple Choice Questions</h3><p style='font-style:italic;color:#555;margin-bottom:8px;page-break-after:avoid;'>Note: Select the most appropriate option for each of the following questions.</p><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q1.</strong> Which of the following packages is automatically imported into every Java program and contains all the standard wrapper classes? </div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) java.io</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) java.util</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) java.lang</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) java.awt</li></ul><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q2.</strong> What is a wrapper class in Java? </div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) A class that wraps standard methods into a single interface</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) A class whose object wraps or contains primitive data types</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) A class used to create graphical user interfaces</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) A subclass of java.util.Scanner</li></ul><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q3.</strong> Which primitive data type corresponds to the wrapper class `Character`? </div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) string</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) String</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) char</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) Character</li></ul><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q4.</strong> The automatic conversion of a primitive data type into its corresponding wrapper class object is known as: </div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) Type casting</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) Unboxing</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) Autoboxing</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) Implicit coercion</li></ul><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q5.</strong> The automatic conversion of a wrapper class object into its corresponding primitive data type is called: </div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) Autoboxing</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) Unboxing</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) Dynamic binding</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) Parsing</li></ul><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q6.</strong> What is the return type of the method `Character.isDigit(char ch)`? </div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) int</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) char</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) String</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) boolean</li></ul><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q7.</strong> What is the output of `Integer.parseInt("250") + 50`? </div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) "25050"</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) 300</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) 25050</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) Error</li></ul><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q8.</strong> Which of the following method calls converts the character `'m'` to `'M'`? </div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) `Character.toUpperCase('m')`</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) `Character.toUpper('m')`</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) `Character.isUpperCase('m')`</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) `Character.parseUpper('m')`</li></ul><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q9.</strong> Which wrapper class method is used to convert a String representation of a decimal number into a primitive double value? </div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) `Double.toDouble(String s)`</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) `Double.convertDouble(String s)`</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) `Double.parseDouble(String s)`</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) `Double.valueOfDouble(String s)`</li></ul><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q10.</strong> What does `Character.isWhitespace(' ')` evaluate to? </div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) false</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) true</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) 0</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) 1</li></ul><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q11.</strong> Which of the following is NOT a valid wrapper class name in Java? </div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) Byte</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) Short</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) Int</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) Float</li></ul><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q12.</strong> What will be the result of `Character.toLowerCase('7')`? </div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) '7'</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) 0</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) false</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) Compilation Error</li></ul><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q13.</strong> What will `Character.isLetterOrDigit('#')` return? </div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) true</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) false</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) null</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) Compilation Error</li></ul><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q14.</strong> Which method converts an integer value to its equivalent String object? </div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) `Integer.parseString(45)`</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) `Integer.toString(45)`</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) `Integer.convertString(45)`</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) `Integer.getInteger(45)`</li></ul><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q15.</strong> Which superclass directly or indirectly acts as the parent class for numeric wrapper classes like `Byte`, `Short`, `Integer`, `Long`, `Float`, and `Double`? </div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) java.lang.Math</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) java.lang.Number</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) java.lang.Object</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) Both (b) and (c)</li></ul><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q16.</strong> Which exception is thrown when `Integer.parseInt("12A3")` is executed? </div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) `ClassCastException`</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) `NullPointerException`</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) `NumberFormatException`</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) `IllegalArgumentException`</li></ul><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q17.</strong> What will be the output of `System.out.println(Character.isUpperCase('K'));`? </div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) 'K'</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) 'k'</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) true</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) false</li></ul><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q18.</strong> Which statement correctly demonstrates explicit unboxing in Java? </div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) `Integer obj = 10;`</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) `int x = obj.intValue();`</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) `Integer obj = Integer.valueOf(10);`</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) `int x = (int)"10";`</li></ul><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q19.</strong> What is the default initial value of an uninitialized object reference of a wrapper class inside a class declaration? </div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) 0</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) 0.0</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) false</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) null</li></ul><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q20.</strong> Which of the following statements about wrapper class objects is TRUE? </div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) Wrapper class objects are mutable.</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) Wrapper class objects are immutable.</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) Wrapper class objects cannot be stored in collection framework structures.</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) Primitive types take more memory than wrapper class objects.</li></ul><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q21.</strong> What is the result of `Float.parseFloat("12.5f") + 0.5f`? </div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) 13.0</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) "12.5f0.5f"</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) 12.50.5</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) Exception</li></ul><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q22.</strong> Which wrapper class is NOT a descendant of the `Number` class? </div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) `Integer`</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) `Double`</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) `Boolean`</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) `Long`</li></ul><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q23.</strong> What does `Character.isLetter('9')` return? </div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) true</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) false</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) '9'</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) 9</li></ul><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q24.</strong> Which of the following is a valid method call to convert a primitive `float` into a `Float` wrapper class object? </div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) `Float.valueOf(5.5f)`</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) `Float.parseFloat(5.5f)`</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) `Float.toString(5.5f)`</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) `Float.isFloat(5.5f)`</li></ul><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q25.</strong> Evaluate the expression: `Character.isLowerCase('a') && Character.isDigit('5')` </div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) true</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) false</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) Compilation Error</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) Runtime Error</li></ul><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q26.</strong> What will `Boolean.parseBoolean("TRUE")` return? </div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) "TRUE"</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) true</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) false</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) null</li></ul><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q27.</strong> Which of the following methods converts a `Character` object or primitive `char` to lower case? </div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) `Character.toLower()`</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) `Character.toLowerCase(char)`</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) `Character.isLowerCase(char)`</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) `Character.convertLower(char)`</li></ul><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q28.</strong> What is the output of the code snippet below?
__CODE<sub>B</sub>LOCK<sub>0</sub>__ </div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) 100</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) 3</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) 1</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) Error</li></ul><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q29.</strong> Identify the type of wrapper class method: `parseXxx()` (e.g., `parseInt`, `parseDouble`). </div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) Non-static method returning primitive type</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) Static method returning primitive type</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) Static method returning object reference type</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) Non-static method returning String</li></ul><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q30.</strong> What will `Character.isWhitespace('	')` return? </div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) false</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) true</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) '	'</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) Error</li></ul><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q31.</strong> Which constant in the `Integer` class gives the number of bits used to represent an `int` value in two's complement binary form? </div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) `Integer.MAX<sub>V</sub>ALUE`</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) `Integer.MIN<sub>V</sub>ALUE`</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) `Integer.SIZE`</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) `Integer.BYTES`</li></ul><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q32.</strong> Consider the code:
__CODE<sub>B</sub>LOCK<sub>0</sub>__\nWhich feature of Java Class 10 is illustrated here? </div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) Explicit Casting</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) Autoboxing</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) Unboxing</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) Dynamic Method Dispatch</li></ul><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q33.</strong> What is the return type of `Character.toUpperCase(char ch)`? </div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) String</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) boolean</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) char</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) int</li></ul><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q34.</strong> Which of the following is a primitive data type and NOT a wrapper class? </div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) Double</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) Boolean</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) short</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) Character</li></ul><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q35.</strong> What will `Long.parseLong("1000")` return? </div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) String "1000"</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) long value 1000L</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) Long wrapper object</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) boolean true</li></ul><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q36.</strong> What happens when you pass a non-numeric string like `"ABC"` to `Double.parseDouble()`? </div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) Returns 0.0</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) Returns NaN</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) Throws `NumberFormatException`</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) Throws `NullPointerException`</li></ul><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q37.</strong> What will `Character.isLetterOrDigit('9')` return? </div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) true</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) false</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) '9'</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) Error</li></ul><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q38.</strong> Which statement correctly converts an integer primitive `int num = 50;` into an `Integer` object using `valueOf()`? </div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) `Integer obj = Integer.valueOf(num);`</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) `Integer obj = num.valueOf();`</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) `Integer obj = Integer.parseInt(num);`</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) `Integer obj = (Integer)num;`</li></ul><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q39.</strong> What is the output of `System.out.println(Character.isLowerCase('9'));`? </div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) true</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) false</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) '9'</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) Compilation Error</li></ul><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q40.</strong> Which method in the `Character` class is used to check if a character is an uppercase letter? </div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) `Character.isUpper(char ch)`</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) `Character.isUpperCase(char ch)`</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) `Character.toUpperCase(char ch)`</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) `Character.checkUpper(char ch)`</li></ul><h3 class='sec-banner' style='margin-top:16px;color:#1e1b4b;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;padding-bottom:4px;page-break-after:avoid;'>Section B: Fill in the Blanks</h3><p style='font-style:italic;color:#555;margin-bottom:8px;page-break-after:avoid;'>Note: Fill in the blanks with appropriate Java terms or statements.</p><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q1.</strong> The process of automatically converting a primitive data type into an object of its corresponding wrapper class is called _______. </div><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q2.</strong> All wrapper classes in Java belong to the _______ package. </div><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q3.</strong> The method used to convert a String into a primitive integer is _______. </div>
